1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Facing different directions
Each hunter sees a limited area in front of their eyes.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
The stag disappears into grass
Grass conceals the stag. No footprints are visible inside it.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
A points — but B has not seen it
A pointing gesture can only be seen when the sender is visible.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
B turns to see A’s gesture
The arm conveys a direction. No distant target cell is highlighted.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Following the indicated direction
B must move and look to find evidence in their own visual field.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The footprint comes into view
The trace becomes visible through B’s own eyes, not through the signal.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Approaching the hiding place
Both hunters approach the same area; the stag remains concealed.
